WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/settings/components/ActiveSessionsSection.tsx — the active-sessions / device-management
  GlassPanel rendered under <section id="security"> on the Settings page. THREE top-level branches:
    1. Loading       — <GlassPanel><Spinner/> "Loading sessions…"</GlassPanel> (placeholder INSIDE the panel
                       chrome so the layout doesn't reflow when data arrives).
    2. Open-mode     — backend reported 501 AUTH_MODE_OPEN ⇒ per-device sessions can't be tracked; inline
                       amber AlertTriangle + "Active sessions" heading + forward-auth helper message.
    3. Forward-auth  — header (Laptop IconBox + "Active sessions" + subtitle) + (hasOthers ? secondary
                       "Sign out all other devices" button, "Signing out…" while pending) + (isError ?
                       inline ErrorText) + DataTable[device(+"This device" badge) / IP / Signed in / Last seen
                       / per-row "Sign out" (hidden for the current row, disabled while that row revokes)].
  Two ConfirmDialogs (per-row "Sign out this device?" + bulk "Sign out all other devices?"), NO silenceKey —
  security primitives ALWAYS confirm. describeDevice(user_agent) is a dependency-free browser/OS match ladder.
  Hooks: useSessions (GET /auth/sessions → {mode:'open'} | {mode:'session',sessions}), useRevokeSession
  (DELETE /auth/sessions/{id}), useRevokeAllOtherSessions (DELETE /auth/sessions/all-others), useTranslation,
  useDateFormat.

