  WHY DEFERRED (full-app Xcode gate — ZERO ActiveSessionsSection errors; all blockers pre-exist this change):
    iOS  : the TeslaSync app target fails at module-dependency resolution on the FIRST co-located feature-view
           test file — "AcDcStatsPanel.Tests.swift:19:8: error: unable to resolve module dependency: 'XCTest'".
           Every Section surface co-locates a `*.Tests.swift` (`import XCTest` + `@testable import TeslaSync`)
           in the app-target source group; ActiveSessionsSection follows that same dominant convention, and the
           build never reaches it (AcDcStatsPanel sorts first). This is the documented "co-located *.Tests.swift
           importing XCTest into the app target" blocker. grep "ActiveSessionsSection.*error:" /tmp/ios-build.log
           = 0 hits.
    macOS: additionally fails before compilation on development SIGNING — "'TeslaSync-macOS' has entitlements
           that require signing with a development certificate" (also TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS), which this runner
           does not provision. grep "ActiveSessionsSection.*error:" /tmp/mac-build.log = 0 hits.
    These are exactly the artifacts apps/macos-pending-verifications.md defers to the ADR-012 macos-latest CI
    runner, owned by the P4/P99 Apple acceptance gate (test-target/app-target separation + signing/archive) —
    NOT by a single feature-view prompt (task rule: do not fix pre-existing unrelated breakage). The same two
    deferrals are recorded by predecessor P4 surfaces (e.g. ToolCard 0010).

